  "question": {
    "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> are two forms of nitrogen dioxide. One exists in gaseous state while other in liquid state. The nature of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> forms are",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ZpZxE",
      "text": "both are paramagnetic",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "aXclr",
      "text": "both are diamagnetic",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lQrbs",
      "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is paramagnetic while <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> is diamagnetic",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "H0SzK",
      "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is diamagnetic while <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> is paramagnetic",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is an odd electron molecule so <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is paramagnetic<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/51f9509a-f672-4600-a0f3-fb99d2b82b81.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:0.99167in;height:0.84167in\" /><br />The dimer, <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> , has no unpaired electron so it is diamagnetic.<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/749370e6-a114-4c81-88c5-f09eae10e37b.jpeg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:1.38333in;height:0.775in\" />",
